---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Brand from '../../components/Brand.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import TechList from '../../components/TechList.astro';
import TensorPlayground from '../../components/TensorPlayground';
import fallback from '../../assets/projects/tensorview/cube.png';
import explorer from '../../assets/projects/tensorview/explorer.png';
import learning from '../../assets/projects/tensorview/learning.png';
import '../../styles/editorial.css';
import '../../styles/tensorview-project.css';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="TensorView — Curtis Ray"
  description="An interactive tool for learning and visualizing tensors. Explore the design, try a small 3D preview, and see how TensorView connects numbers to space."
>
  <main id="main" class="tensor-project">
    <div class="tensor-cover">
      <nav class="tensor-topbar" aria-label="Portfolio navigation">
        <Brand />
        <a class="tensor-label underline-link" href="/#work-tensorview">
          ← My work
        </a>
      </nav>
      <header class="tensor-heading">
        <div>
          <p class="tensor-label">Personal project / 2026</p>
          <h1>TensorView</h1>
          <p class="tensor-tagline">Making tensors tangible.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="tensor-intro">
          <p>
            A tool for learning and visualizing tensors. Turn an array of
            numbers into something you can see, move, and understand.
          </p>
          <a
            class="tensor-label underline-link"
            href="https://tensorview.curtisray.me"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
          >
            Open TensorView ↗
          </a>
        </div>
      </header>
      <TensorPlayground fallback={fallback.src} client:visible />
      <p class="tensor-preview-note tensor-label">
        A little piece to play with. The full explorer and lessons live in
        TensorView.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="tensor-story">
      <section class="tensor-section" aria-labelledby="idea-title">
        <p class="tensor-label">01 / The idea</p>
        <div class="tensor-copy">
          <h2 id="idea-title">
            From a number
            <br />
            to a space.
          </h2>
          <p>
            Tensors can feel abstract when you meet them as notation. TensorView
            gives those numbers a shape, starting with a single value and
            building toward a three-dimensional array.
          </p>
          <p>
            Color reveals the values. Layers reveal the structure. Changing a
            number shows how the representations relate.
          </p>
        </div>
        <ol class="tensor-progression" aria-label="From scalar to tensor">
          <li>
            <span class="tensor-symbol" aria-hidden="true">
              •
            </span>
            <h3>Scalar</h3>
            <p>One value.</p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="tensor-symbol" aria-hidden="true">
              →
            </span>
            <h3>Vector</h3>
            <p>A line of values.</p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="tensor-symbol" aria-hidden="true">
              ▦
            </span>
            <h3>Matrix</h3>
            <p>A grid of values.</p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <svg class="tensor-symbol" viewBox="0 0 80 80" aria-hidden="true">
              <g fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1">
                <path d="M40 8 70 25 70 58 40 75 10 58 10 25Z M10 25 40 42 70 25 M40 42V75 M25 17 55 34V67 M55 17 25 34V67 M10 36 40 53 70 36 M10 47 40 64 70 47" />
              </g>
            </svg>
            <h3>Tensor</h3>
            <p>A stack of grids.</p>
          </li>
        </ol>
      </section>
      <section class="tensor-section" aria-labelledby="explorer-title">
        <p class="tensor-label">02 / The explorer</p>
        <div class="tensor-copy">
          <h2 id="explorer-title">
            Three views.
            <br />
            One shared dataset.
          </h2>
          <p>
            A two-dimensional slice, a 3D volume, and an editable numerical grid
            stay in sync. Select a cell in one view and find it in the others;
            edit its value and watch the colors change.
          </p>
          <p>
            Scrub through time, play a wave, or separate the layers to see how a
            slice fits inside the whole. Presets offer a starting point, with
            custom formulas for further exploration.
          </p>
        </div>
        <figure class="tensor-wide">
          <Image
            src={explorer}
            alt="TensorView’s explorer shows a color-coded slice, a three-dimensional tensor, and its editable numerical values side by side."
            widths={[600, 1000, 1440, 2000, 2880]}
            quality={90}
            sizes="94vw"
          />
          <figcaption>
            Spatial, visual, and numerical representations of the same tensor.
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
      </section>
      <section class="tensor-section" aria-labelledby="learning-title">
        <p class="tensor-label">03 / Learning by doing</p>
        <div class="tensor-copy">
          <h2 id="learning-title">
            Build the intuition.
            <br />
            Then explore.
          </h2>
          <p>
            A guided introduction moves from scalars to vectors, matrices, and
            third-order tensors, then explains slices and fibers. Each step
            pairs an interactive visual with the corresponding notation.
          </p>
          <p>
            The goal is to make the relationship between dimensions and data
            easier to grasp before opening the full explorer.
          </p>
        </div>
        <figure class="tensor-wide">
          <Image
            src={learning}
            alt="TensorView’s guided lesson pairs a three-dimensional tensor visualization with an explanation of its dimensions and indexing."
            widths={[600, 1000, 1440, 2000, 2880]}
            quality={90}
            sizes="94vw"
          />
          <figcaption>
            A step-by-step path from a single value to a multidimensional array.
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
      </section>
      <section class="tensor-section" aria-labelledby="build-title">
        <p class="tensor-label">04 / The build</p>
        <div class="tensor-copy">
          <h2 id="build-title">
            A small stack.
            <br />A shared source of truth.
          </h2>
          <p>
            Built with vanilla JavaScript, Three.js, and Vite. A shared tensor
            model stores the values and notifies each view when they change.
            Three.js renders the volume, a 2D canvas draws the slice, and
            MathJax handles the mathematical notation.
          </p>
          <TechList items={['three', 'vite']} compact />
          <div class="tensor-links">
            <a
              class="tensor-label underline-link"
              href="https://tensorview.curtisray.me"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
            >
              Open TensorView ↗
            </a>
            <a
              class="tensor-label underline-link"
              href="https://github.com/curtisray/tensorview"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
            >
              View source ↗
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
      <div class="tensor-endnote">
        <p class="tensor-label">Designed & built by Curtis Ray</p>
        <a class="tensor-label underline-link" href="/work/people">
          Next project: People the App ↗
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
